diff --git a/docs/live-game.md b/docs/live-game.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6b54522
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/live-game.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Live game implementation notes
+
+- A quiz run is a separate `games` row with a random five-character join code. Starting a run snapshots only active questions and their options into `game_questions` / `game_options`, so later moderator edits do not alter an in-progress game and two runs never share players or answers.
+- The game moves through `waiting -> open -> closed -> open ... -> over`. Moderator actions are conditional database updates; the final `Next` action ends the run. An all-inactive quiz cannot be started.
+- Player identities are anonymous. A random per-player token is held in an HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax cookie scoped to that game's URL. Re-opening a join link resumes the player; a game that is over never creates a new player.
+- Player answer reads are deliberately separate from moderator result reads. While a question is open, player JSON contains only option IDs and text, the player's selected option, and the question. It has no correctness field or answer totals. The moderator result endpoint only includes correctness and per-option totals after `Finish`.
+- Moderator and player pages use no-cache JSON polls (250 ms while the game is live or showing results) and update their DOM in place, with a short retry cadence to recover from Wi-Fi interruptions. The server timestamps question openings and each answer pick so scoring and speed tie-breaks use a shared clock. The QR code is rendered locally as SVG from the same HTTP join URL shown as text; the app does not call an external QR or other service.
+- All persisted game state is in the same SQLite database under `storage/`; the release/start path builds dependencies offline.
+- Per-question timing is configured on the quiz (minutes plus seconds) and intentionally omitted from `QuizTransfer`. A newly created game snapshots that duration in `games`; each question uses its existing persisted `opened_at_ms` as the deadline origin, so reloading the moderator screen cannot reset it. The moderator screen renders the remaining time and submits the normal `Finish` action at zero; a lightweight server worker also closes due questions if the screen is not open, while player state never includes timer data.
diff --git a/docs/prizes.md b/docs/prizes.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bd5af04
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/prizes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# Scoring and prizes
+
+- `quizzes.number_of_winners` is an integer of at least one (default 3). A game snapshots this value when it is created, just as it snapshots its questions, so later settings edits do not change a live run.
+- A player's score is derived from their final answer for each question. Correct answers each award one point; answer changes replace the previous pick. Player APIs omit aggregate scores and places until the game is over.
+- The server records `game_questions.opened_at_ms` when a question opens and `answers.answered_at_ms` on every accepted pick. Equal-point standings sum only the elapsed time of correct final answers, then use player ID as a deterministic final tie-break.
+- The completed game's leaderboard and phone results are derived from those same standings. Winner flags are stored on the game's players and are re-read by the existing no-cache 250 ms state polls, so both result screens update after each prize action.
+- “Top N” takes the first N positive scorers in leaderboard order. “Draw” keeps every score above the cutoff and chooses the remaining winners randomly from all players tied on the cutoff score (ignoring speed); it never selects a zero-score player. If there are fewer positive scorers than prizes, all positive scorers win. “Reset winners” clears all flags.
+- Database initialization adds the prize and timing columns to existing SQLite databases as well as new ones. The quiz import/export JSON remains unchanged; imported quizzes use the default of three winners.
diff --git a/src/live.rs b/src/live.rs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..14cb93c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/live.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,2253 @@
+use super::{AppState, Quiz, csrf_error, escape_html, internal_error, open_database, page};
+use axum::Json;
+use axum::extract::{Form, Path, State};
+use axum::http::{HeaderMap, HeaderValue, StatusCode, header};
+use axum::response::{Html, IntoResponse, Redirect, Response};
+use qrcode::{Color as QrColor, QrCode};
+use rusqlite::{OptionalExtension, params};
+use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
+use std::fs::File;
+use std::io::Read;
+use std::path::{Path as FsPath, PathBuf};
+use std::time::{Duration, SystemTime, UNIX_EPOCH};
+
+const CODE_ALPHABET: &[u8] = b"ABCDEFGHJKLMNPQRSTUVWXYZ23456789";
+const COOKIE_PREFIX: &str = "quizzy_player_";
+
+#[derive(Deserialize)]
+pub(super) struct CsrfForm {
+    #[serde(default)]
+    csrf: String,
+}
+
+#[derive(Deserialize)]
+pub(super) struct JoinForm {
+    #[serde(default)]
+    name: String,
+}
+
+#[derive(Deserialize)]
+pub(super) struct GameActionForm {
+    #[serde(default)]
+    csrf: String,
+    #[serde(default)]
+    action: String,
+}
+
+#[derive(Deserialize)]
+pub(super) struct AnswerForm {
+    option_id: i64,
+}
+
+#[derive(Serialize, Clone)]
+struct GameOptionState {
+    id: i64,
+    text: String,
+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
+    answers: Option<i64>,
+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
+    correct: Option<bool>,
+}
+
+#[derive(Serialize, Clone)]
+struct ModeratorGameState {
+    status: String,
+    title: String,
+    code: String,
+    join_url: String,
+    players: i64,
+    number_of_winners: i64,
+    current_position: Option<i64>,
+    question_number: Option<i64>,
+    question_count: i64,
+    question_text: Option<String>,
+    answered: i64,
+    timer_remaining_ms: Option<i64>,
+    options: Vec<GameOptionState>,
+    leaderboard: Vec<LeaderboardEntry>,
+}
+
+#[derive(Serialize, Clone)]
+struct LeaderboardEntry {
+    place: i64,
+    name: String,
+    points: i64,
+    is_winner: bool,
+}
+
+#[derive(Clone)]
+struct RankedPlayer {
+    id: i64,
+    name: String,
+    points: i64,
+    is_winner: bool,
+}
+
+#[derive(Serialize)]
+struct PlayerOption {
+    id: i64,
+    text: String,
+}
+
+#[derive(Serialize)]
+struct PlayerQuestion {
+    id: i64,
+    text: String,
+    options: Vec<PlayerOption>,
+}
+
+#[derive(Serialize)]
+struct PlayerGameState {
+    status: String,
+    player_name: String,
+    question_number: Option<i64>,
+    question_count: i64,
+    question: Option<PlayerQuestion>,
+    selected_option: Option<i64>,
+    feedback: Option<String>,
+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
+    place: Option<i64>,
+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
+    player_count: Option<i64>,
+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
+    points: Option<i64>,
+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
+    is_winner: Option<bool>,
+}
+
+#[derive(Serialize)]
+struct AnswerAck {
+    ok: bool,
+}
+
+fn canonical_code(raw: &str) -> Option<String> {
+    if raw.len() != 5
+        || !raw
+            .bytes()
+            .all(|byte| CODE_ALPHABET.contains(&byte.to_ascii_uppercase()))
+    {
+        return None;
+    }
+    Some(raw.to_ascii_uppercase())
+}
+
+fn secure_random_bytes(length: usize) -> std::io::Result<Vec<u8>> {
+    let mut bytes = vec![0; length];
+    File::open("/dev/urandom")?.read_exact(&mut bytes)?;
+    Ok(bytes)
+}
+
+fn new_game_code() -> std::io::Result<String> {
+    let random = secure_random_bytes(5)?;
+    Ok(random
+        .iter()
+        .map(|byte| CODE_ALPHABET[usize::from(*byte) % CODE_ALPHABET.len()] as char)
+        .collect())
+}
+
+fn new_player_token() -> std::io::Result<String> {
+    let random = secure_random_bytes(32)?;
+    Ok(random.iter().map(|byte| format!("{byte:02x}")).collect())
+}
+
+fn now_ms() -> i64 {
+    SystemTime::now()
+        .duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH)
+        .unwrap_or_default()
+        .as_millis()
+        .min(i64::MAX as u128) as i64
+}
+
+fn expire_due_game(
+    connection: &rusqlite::Connection,
+    game_id: i64,
+    now: i64,
+) -> rusqlite::Result<bool> {
+    let due: bool = connection.query_row(
+        "SELECT EXISTS(
+             SELECT 1 FROM games game
+             JOIN game_questions question
+               ON question.game_id = game.id AND question.position = game.current_position
+             WHERE game.id = ?1 AND game.status = 'open' AND game.timer_duration_ms > 0
+               AND question.opened_at_ms IS NOT NULL
+               AND question.opened_at_ms <= ?2 - game.timer_duration_ms
+         )",
+        params![game_id, now],
+        |row| row.get(0),
+    )?;
+    if !due {
+        return Ok(false);
+    }
+    Ok(connection.execute(
+        "UPDATE games SET status = 'closed'
+         WHERE id = ?1 AND status = 'open' AND timer_duration_ms > 0
+           AND EXISTS(
+               SELECT 1 FROM game_questions question
+               WHERE question.game_id = games.id
+                 AND question.position = games.current_position
+                 AND question.opened_at_ms IS NOT NULL
+                 AND question.opened_at_ms <= ?2 - games.timer_duration_ms
+           )",
+        params![game_id, now],
+    )? == 1)
+}
+
+fn expire_due_games(connection: &rusqlite::Connection, now: i64) -> rusqlite::Result<usize> {
+    let due: bool = connection.query_row(
+        "SELECT EXISTS(
+             SELECT 1 FROM games game
+             JOIN game_questions question
+               ON question.game_id = game.id AND question.position = game.current_position
+             WHERE game.status = 'open' AND game.timer_duration_ms > 0
+               AND question.opened_at_ms IS NOT NULL
+               AND question.opened_at_ms <= ?1 - game.timer_duration_ms
+         )",
+        [now],
+        |row| row.get(0),
+    )?;
+    if !due {
+        return Ok(0);
+    }
+    connection.execute(
+        "UPDATE games SET status = 'closed'
+         WHERE status = 'open' AND timer_duration_ms > 0
+           AND EXISTS(
+               SELECT 1 FROM game_questions question
+               WHERE question.game_id = games.id
+                 AND question.position = games.current_position
+                 AND question.opened_at_ms IS NOT NULL
+                 AND question.opened_at_ms <= ?1 - games.timer_duration_ms
+           )",
+        [now],
+    )
+}
+
+pub(super) fn start_timer_worker(path: PathBuf) -> std::io::Result<()> {
+    std::thread::Builder::new()
+        .name("quizzy-question-timer".to_owned())
+        .spawn(move || {
+            loop {
+                match open_database(&path)
+                    .and_then(|connection| expire_due_games(&connection, now_ms()).map(|_| ()))
+                {
+                    Ok(()) => {}
+                    Err(error) => eprintln!("Quizzy timer worker: {error}"),
+                }
+                std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(100));
+            }
+        })?;
+    Ok(())
+}
